<!--
  RM_SapSuckerGuild.xml                            FEVERWOOD_SAP_SUCKER_GUILD_1

  The sap-drinker guild's four members (fever_wood_deep_and_mud_2026-09-23.md
  §6/§6g/§6n; the exact defNames/labels/silhouettes below are already
  authored, not invented here, by fever_wood_fauna_roster_2026-09-23.md §2 —
  this item builds what that roster named). One rule, four expressions:
  "clamped to bark, drinks sap, does not flee... they differ only in how
  they refuse to be bothered." All four are herdable and taming does NOT
  disarm the refusal (§6n) — every comp below fires regardless of tame
  status, since it triggers on the pawn taking damage, not on faction.

  1. RM_Thornbug — the nectar contract (existing)  -> RM_ThornbugNectar (live gather)
  2. RM_Vaulm    — seals in hardened sap           -> RM_VaulmLacquer (butcher only)
  3. RM_Ollareth — screams for help                -> nothing directly, an alarm
  4. RM_Drommath — swells until it can't be pulled -> RM_DrommathSap + burst payout

  RM_Thornbug is the ThingDef/PawnKindDef precedent
  FEVER_WOOD_MECHANICS_1's own F8 build flagged as missing for
  RM_CompGatherableCalmGated ("This item owns creating that precedent" —
  this item's own file) — the comp itself is untouched, already compiling.

  RM_Ollareth's scream reuses RimMandrake.CreatureBehaviors'
  RM_CompProperties_PlantAlarm (ROT_GUARDIAN_GROVES_1) rather than a new
  class: that comp already does exactly "sets nearby tagged responders to
  Manhunter toward the disturbance, cooldown-gated, mod-setting-gated" —
  the same shape as "sets the chorus off, pulls the crown's predators
  toward whatever is bothering it" — content-blind (no species hardcoded),
  and mandrake.rm.creaturebehaviors is already a hard modDependency/
  loadAfter of this mod's own About.xml. ⚠️ No RM_AlarmResponderExtension
  is tagged onto any Fever Wood race yet — the crown's own predator
  (RM_Silloch, fauna roster row 7) is not built by any item yet, and the
  current wait-ambush occupant is the Star Wars-tier RSW_LongtailGorg
  (WildAnimals_FeverWood.xml, RUT layer) which this franchise-free RM mod
  may not reference (Q11a). So this pass wires the trigger for real but it
  currently has zero responders to wake — the same "proved, not yet wired"
  posture FEVER_WOOD_MECHANICS_1's own F2 shipped in. Tagging
  RM_Silloch (or, on the RUT/RSW patch layer, RSW_LongtailGorg) with
  <RM_AlarmResponderExtension><tag>FeverWoodCrown</tag></RM_AlarmResponderExtension>
  is that future roster/patch item's own one-line finish, not invented here.

  Vaulm/drommath use the new local RM_CompProperties_SapSuckerRefusal (this
  mod, RM_CompSapSuckerRefusal.cs) — see that class for why a shared hediff-
  refusal comp beat tripling the fear-scan pattern.

  🔴 Deferred, not guessed: §6n's OTHER refusal trigger ("mishandled" during
  a failed taming/training attempt, alongside "frightened") — which job/
  interaction hook fires on a failed handling attempt is a real engine
  question this pass could not verify (RimSage does not connect from this
  machine) and did not want to invent. What ships instead is the trigger
  this pass COULD verify for real: every member's refusal fires on taking
  damage, deterministically, cooldown-gated, never a random roll (the
  design doc's own explicit requirement). FEVERWOOD_SAP_SUCKER_TUNING_1
  owns the mishandling half, plus every INVENTED stat/value in this file
  and its sibling Hediff/Item defs — none of the numbers below are ruled.

  Body: BeetleLike (11 existing repo uses for small insectoid fauna,
  Greentide's own RM_GreatboleGrub among them) — the guild's own legibility
  matrix (fauna roster §6) reads all four by SILHOUETTE state (a thorn, a
  resin bead, a vent, a swelling sac), not by skeleton, so body plan only
  gates health/damage here, never the sprite.

  Art: RM_Thornbug ships REAL finished art — three already-generated,
  validated (registry.jsonl: "verdict": "pass") facings at
  infrastructure/artpipe/_artsrc/feverwood_thornbug_{south,east,north}/,
  found by searching artpipe done/_artsrc/registry.jsonl for "thornbug"
  FIRST per the standing rule, copied into this mod's own Textures/ rather
  than regenerated. RM_Vaulm/RM_Ollareth/RM_Drommath ship flat-color
  placeholder PNGs (128x128, Graphic_Single, same posture as
  RM_Sekkulaath_Juvenile) — searched the same three sources for "vaulm"/
  "ollareth"/"drommath" first; nothing exists. Real bespoke art for all
  three is owed to the standing art pipeline.
-->
<Defs>

  <ThingDef Name="RM_SapSuckerBase" ParentName="AnimalThingBase" Abstract="true">
    <statBases>
      <!-- INVENTED placeholders, all four rows: small clamped bark-dwellers,
           deliberately sluggish rather than fleeing (§6's "does not flee"
           read as the closest safe engine approximation — a genuinely
           locked-in-place animal risks breaking core taming/herding AI). -->
      <MoveSpeed>1.6</MoveSpeed>
      <ComfyTemperatureMin>10</ComfyTemperatureMin>
      <ComfyTemperatureMax>45</ComfyTemperatureMax>
      <Flammability>1.0</Flammability>
      <Wildness>0.4</Wildness>
    </statBases>
    <tools>
      <li>
        <label>mandibles</label>
        <capacities>
          <li>Bite</li>
        </capacities>
        <power>3</power>
        <cooldownTime>2.2</cooldownTime>
        <linkedBodyPartsGroup>Mouth</linkedBodyPartsGroup>
      </li>
    </tools>
    <race>
      <body>BeetleLike</body>
      <herdAnimal>false</herdAnimal>
      <predator>false</predator>
      <baseBodySize>0.25</baseBodySize>
      <baseHealthScale>0.55</baseHealthScale>
      <baseHungerRate>0.6</baseHungerRate>
      <foodType>VegetarianRoughAnimal</foodType>
      <manhunterOnDamageChance>0</manhunterOnDamageChance>
      <!-- §6n: "all four are herdable" — tamable, not vermin-only. -->
      <manhunterOnTameFailChance>0.1</manhunterOnTameFailChance>
      <trainability>Intermediate</trainability>
      <fleshType>Insectoid</fleshType>
      <bloodDef>Filth_BloodInsect</bloodDef>
      <bloodSmearDef>Filth_BloodSmear</bloodSmearDef>
      <gestationPeriodDays>2</gestationPeriodDays>
      <litterSizeCurve>
        <points>
          <li>(0.99, 0)</li>
          <li>(1, 1)</li>
          <li>(2, 1)</li>
          <li>(2.01, 0)</li>
        </points>
      </litterSizeCurve>
      <lifeExpectancy>5</lifeExpectancy>
      <lifeStageAges>
        <li>
          <def>AnimalBaby</def>
          <minAge>0</minAge>
        </li>
        <li>
          <def>AnimalJuvenile</def>
          <minAge>0.2</minAge>
        </li>
        <li>
          <def>AnimalAdult</def>
          <minAge>0.4</minAge>
          <soundWounded>Pawn_Insect_Ambient</soundWounded>
          <soundDeath>Pawn_Insect_Ambient</soundDeath>
        </li>
      </lifeStageAges>
      <soundMeleeHitPawn>Pawn_Melee_SmallScratch_HitPawn</soundMeleeHitPawn>
      <soundMeleeHitBuilding>Pawn_Melee_SmallScratch_HitBuilding</soundMeleeHitBuilding>
      <soundMeleeMiss>Pawn_Melee_SmallScratch_Miss</soundMeleeMiss>
      <soundEating>Insectoid_Eat</soundEating>
    </race>
    <tradeTags>
      <li>AnimalInsect</li>
    </tradeTags>
  </ThingDef>

  <!-- ============================================================ -->
  <!-- 1. RM_Thornbug — the nectar contract (existing lore, new def)  -->
  <!-- ============================================================ -->

  <ThingDef ParentName="RM_SapSuckerBase">
    <defName>RM_Thornbug</defName>
    <label>thornbug</label>
    <description>A great thorn-shaped insect clamped flush to the bark, secreting sweet, nourishing nectar in exchange for safety. The mechanic is the deal: it yields only while it feels safe, and a frightened herd dries up for days. Every raid on the crown costs nectar before it costs blood.</description>
    <statBases>
      <MarketValue>140</MarketValue>
    </statBases>
    <comps>
      <li Class="RimMandrake.EnvironmentalHazards.RM_CompProperties_GatherableCalmGated" MayRequire="mandrake.rm.environmentalhazards">
        <gatherDef>RM_ThornbugNectar</gatherDef>
      </li>
    </comps>
  </ThingDef>

  <PawnKindDef ParentName="AnimalKindBase">
    <defName>RM_Thornbug</defName>
    <label>thornbug</label>
    <race>RM_Thornbug</race>
    <combatPower>15</combatPower>
    <canArriveManhunter>false</canArriveManhunter>
    <wildGroupSize>2~5</wildGroupSize>
    <lifeStages>
      <li>
        <bodyGraphicData>
          <texPath>Things/Pawn/Animal/RM_Thornbug/RM_Thornbug</texPath>
          <graphicClass>Graphic_Multi</graphicClass>
          <drawSize>0.5</drawSize>
        </bodyGraphicData>
      </li>
      <li>
        <bodyGraphicData>
          <texPath>Things/Pawn/Animal/RM_Thornbug/RM_Thornbug</texPath>
          <graphicClass>Graphic_Multi</graphicClass>
          <drawSize>0.65</drawSize>
        </bodyGraphicData>
      </li>
      <li>
        <bodyGraphicData>
          <texPath>Things/Pawn/Animal/RM_Thornbug/RM_Thornbug</texPath>
          <graphicClass>Graphic_Multi</graphicClass>
          <drawSize>0.8</drawSize>
        </bodyGraphicData>
      </li>
    </lifeStages>
  </PawnKindDef>

  <!-- ============================================================ -->
  <!-- 2. RM_Vaulm — seals itself in hardened sap                     -->
  <!-- ============================================================ -->

  <ThingDef ParentName="RM_SapSuckerBase">
    <defName>RM_Vaulm</defName>
    <label>vaulm</label>
    <description>A smooth swollen bead of amber on the bark, no limbs visible. Bothered, it floods its own shell and sets — armour, not flesh — and must be cracked open before anything more can be done to it. Killing and cracking it open yields a usable lacquer.</description>
    <statBases>
      <MarketValue>110</MarketValue>
    </statBases>
    <race>
      <!-- "must be cracked open to reach [the lacquer]" — a butcher-only
           yield, never a live gather. -->
      <leatherDef>RM_VaulmLacquer</leatherDef>
    </race>
    <comps>
      <li Class="RimMandrake.FeverWood.RM_CompProperties_SapSuckerRefusal">
        <refusalHediff>RM_Hediff_SapSealed</refusalHediff>
      </li>
    </comps>
  </ThingDef>

  <PawnKindDef ParentName="AnimalKindBase">
    <defName>RM_Vaulm</defName>
    <label>vaulm</label>
    <race>RM_Vaulm</race>
    <combatPower>12</combatPower>
    <canArriveManhunter>false</canArriveManhunter>
    <wildGroupSize>1~3</wildGroupSize>
    <lifeStages>
      <li>
        <bodyGraphicData>
          <texPath>Things/Pawn/Animal/RM_Vaulm/RM_Vaulm</texPath>
          <graphicClass>Graphic_Single</graphicClass>
          <drawSize>0.4</drawSize>
        </bodyGraphicData>
      </li>
      <li>
        <bodyGraphicData>
          <texPath>Things/Pawn/Animal/RM_Vaulm/RM_Vaulm</texPath>
          <graphicClass>Graphic_Single</graphicClass>
          <drawSize>0.55</drawSize>
        </bodyGraphicData>
      </li>
      <li>
        <bodyGraphicData>
          <texPath>Things/Pawn/Animal/RM_Vaulm/RM_Vaulm</texPath>
          <graphicClass>Graphic_Single</graphicClass>
          <drawSize>0.7</drawSize>
        </bodyGraphicData>
      </li>
    </lifeStages>
  </PawnKindDef>

  <!-- ============================================================ -->
  <!-- 3. RM_Ollareth — screams for help                              -->
  <!-- ============================================================ -->

  <ThingDef ParentName="RM_SapSuckerBase">
    <defName>RM_Ollareth</defName>
    <label>ollareth</label>
    <description>Flat, wide, and ringed with open spiracles — bothered, it screams, and the whole crown answers. It yields nothing of its own; its value is that the biome fights for it, turning a theft raid into a fight the crown joins on your side.</description>
    <statBases>
      <MarketValue>90</MarketValue>
    </statBases>
    <comps>
      <!-- Reused, not new — see file header. INVENTED radius/cooldown;
           no responder is tagged onto any Fever Wood race yet. -->
      <li Class="RimMandrake.CreatureBehaviors.RM_CompProperties_PlantAlarm" MayRequire="mandrake.rm.creaturebehaviors">
        <radius>24</radius>
        <tag>FeverWoodCrown</tag>
        <cooldownTicks>2500</cooldownTicks>
      </li>
    </comps>
  </ThingDef>

  <PawnKindDef ParentName="AnimalKindBase">
    <defName>RM_Ollareth</defName>
    <label>ollareth</label>
    <race>RM_Ollareth</race>
    <combatPower>10</combatPower>
    <canArriveManhunter>false</canArriveManhunter>
    <wildGroupSize>1~3</wildGroupSize>
    <lifeStages>
      <li>
        <bodyGraphicData>
          <texPath>Things/Pawn/Animal/RM_Ollareth/RM_Ollareth</texPath>
          <graphicClass>Graphic_Single</graphicClass>
          <drawSize>0.4</drawSize>
        </bodyGraphicData>
      </li>
      <li>
        <bodyGraphicData>
          <texPath>Things/Pawn/Animal/RM_Ollareth/RM_Ollareth</texPath>
          <graphicClass>Graphic_Single</graphicClass>
          <drawSize>0.55</drawSize>
        </bodyGraphicData>
      </li>
      <li>
        <bodyGraphicData>
          <texPath>Things/Pawn/Animal/RM_Ollareth/RM_Ollareth</texPath>
          <graphicClass>Graphic_Single</graphicClass>
          <drawSize>0.7</drawSize>
        </bodyGraphicData>
      </li>
    </lifeStages>
  </PawnKindDef>

  <!-- ============================================================ -->
  <!-- 4. RM_Drommath — swells until it cannot be pulled off          -->
  <!-- ============================================================ -->

  <ThingDef ParentName="RM_SapSuckerBase">
    <defName>RM_Drommath</defName>
    <label>drommath</label>
    <description>A taut grey sac, visibly inflating. Handled, it swells rather than yield, until it cannot be pulled from its perch. Left calm, it can be milked for a small trickle of sap; burst instead, it pays out once, large — and never again.</description>
    <statBases>
      <MarketValue>100</MarketValue>
    </statBases>
    <!-- The one-time "burst" payout — plain butcherProducts (a top-level
         ThingDef field, not nested under <race>), no special bookkeeping:
         a butchered drommath simply stops producing RM_DrommathSap for
         good, same as any killed animal. -->
    <butcherProducts>
      <RM_DrommathBurstSap>25</RM_DrommathBurstSap>
    </butcherProducts>
    <comps>
      <!-- The renewable trickle — reuses RM_CompGatherableCalmGated
           (EnvironmentalHazards, F8, already verified/compiling) rather
           than the vanilla generic CompHasGatherableBodyResource/
           CompProperties_HasGatherableBodyResource pair, which has zero
           precedent anywhere in this repo (fauna roster §7's own finding)
           and whose exact XML-exposed field names this pass could not
           verify against source (RimSage does not connect from this
           machine) — reusing a class whose real fields are already read
           straight from its own .cs file beats guessing a vanilla one's.
           calmFloor/fearRadius keep the shared class's own already-ruled
           defaults (card 3, ~40 cells); only gatherDef/amount/interval are
           set per-species here. -->
      <li Class="RimMandrake.EnvironmentalHazards.RM_CompProperties_GatherableCalmGated" MayRequire="mandrake.rm.environmentalhazards">
        <gatherDef>RM_DrommathSap</gatherDef>
        <gatherAmount>10</gatherAmount>
        <gatherIntervalDays>3</gatherIntervalDays>
      </li>
      <li Class="RimMandrake.FeverWood.RM_CompProperties_SapSuckerRefusal">
        <refusalHediff>RM_Hediff_Swollen</refusalHediff>
      </li>
    </comps>
  </ThingDef>

  <PawnKindDef ParentName="AnimalKindBase">
    <defName>RM_Drommath</defName>
    <label>drommath</label>
    <race>RM_Drommath</race>
    <combatPower>10</combatPower>
    <canArriveManhunter>false</canArriveManhunter>
    <wildGroupSize>1~3</wildGroupSize>
    <lifeStages>
      <li>
        <bodyGraphicData>
          <texPath>Things/Pawn/Animal/RM_Drommath/RM_Drommath</texPath>
          <graphicClass>Graphic_Single</graphicClass>
          <drawSize>0.4</drawSize>
        </bodyGraphicData>
      </li>
      <li>
        <bodyGraphicData>
          <texPath>Things/Pawn/Animal/RM_Drommath/RM_Drommath</texPath>
          <graphicClass>Graphic_Single</graphicClass>
          <drawSize>0.6</drawSize>
        </bodyGraphicData>
      </li>
      <li>
        <bodyGraphicData>
          <texPath>Things/Pawn/Animal/RM_Drommath/RM_Drommath</texPath>
          <graphicClass>Graphic_Single</graphicClass>
          <drawSize>0.8</drawSize>
        </bodyGraphicData>
      </li>
    </lifeStages>
  </PawnKindDef>

</Defs>
